{
  "title": "Quadratic Equations — Meet the Mighty ax² + bx + c = 0 💪",
  "hook": "A ball thrown upward follows a path described by a quadratic equation. The area of a rectangular garden, the time taken by two pipes to fill a tank — all lead to equations with x². Welcome to the world of <strong>Quadratic Equations</strong>!",
  "explanation": "<div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#E8F5E9,#C8E6C9);border-radius:12px;padding:16px;margin:10px 0;text-align:center\"><strong style=\"font-size:1.1rem\">Standard Form:</strong> <span style=\"font-size:1.2rem;font-family:serif\">ax² + bx + c = 0</span> where <strong>a ≠ 0</strong></div>\n\n<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Coefficient</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Role</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Example in 3x²−5x+2=0</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">a</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Coefficient of x² (must not be 0!)</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">b</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Coefficient of x</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">−5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">c</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Constant term</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">2</td></tr></table>\n<strong>Solving by Factorization (Splitting the Middle Term):</strong>\n\n<div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#2E7D32;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div>\n<div><strong>Find two numbers</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">whose <strong>sum = b</strong> and <strong>product = a×c</strong></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#2E7D32;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div>\n<div><strong>Split the middle term</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Replace bx with these two numbers</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#2E7D32;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div>\n<div><strong>Factor by grouping</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Take common factors from pairs</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#2E7D32;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div>\n<div><strong>Set each factor = 0</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Solve to get the two roots</span></div></div></div>",
  "worked_example": "<strong>Solve: 6x² − x − 2 = 0</strong>\n\n<div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div>\n<div><strong>Identify a, b, c</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">a = 6, b = −1, c = −2. Product ac = 6 × (−2) = −12</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div>\n<div><strong>Find two numbers</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Sum = −1, Product = −12<br>Numbers: <strong>−4 and 3</strong> (−4 + 3 = −1, −4 × 3 = −12) ✓</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div>\n<div><strong>Split middle term</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">6x² − 4x + 3x − 2 = 0</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div>\n<div><strong>Group and factor</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">2x(3x − 2) + 1(3x − 2) = 0<br>(2x + 1)(3x − 2) = 0</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#1565C0;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">5</div>\n<div><strong>Set each factor = 0</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">2x + 1 = 0 → <strong>x = −1/2</strong><br>3x − 2 = 0 → <strong>x = 2/3</strong></span></div></div></div><div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#E3F2FD,#BBDEFB);border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:1.05rem;text-align:center\">\n<div style=\"font-size:0.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:#1565C0;margin-bottom:4px\">ANSWER</div><strong>Roots: x = −1/2 &nbsp;and&nbsp; x = 2/3</strong></div>",
  "try_this": {
    "question": "Solve by factorization: 2x² + x − 6 = 0",
    "hint": "Find two numbers whose sum = 1 (coefficient of x) and product = 2 × (−6) = −12.",
    "answer": "Numbers: 4 and −3 (sum = 1, product = −12)\n2x² + 4x − 3x − 6 = 0\n2x(x + 2) − 3(x + 2) = 0\n(2x − 3)(x + 2) = 0\nx = 3/2 or x = −2"
  },
  "fun_fact": "The ancient Babylonians were solving quadratic equations as early as 2000 BCE — that's 4000 years ago! They used a geometric method: they literally completed a square using clay tablets. 🏛️"
}